cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file, and/or the paper describing CWatM listed under 'preferred-citation'."
type: software
title: "CWatM - Community Water Model"
abstract: >-
  CWatM (Community Water Model) is a hydrological model that simulates the
  water cycle at daily time steps and at global and local scales, historically
  and into the future. It assesses water supply, water demand and
  environmental needs, including water management and human influence within
  the water cycle. CWatM is developed and maintained by IIASA's Water Security
  group.
